    "Lead" : {
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "Plomo"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Lead can still come from pipes and faucets inside your home, especially in homes built before 1986. Testing your tap for lead is the best way to know." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El plomo todavía puede venir de las tuberías y grifos dentro de su hogar, sobre todo en casas construidas antes de 1986. Analizar el agua del grifo para detectar plomo es la mejor manera de saberlo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Lead depends on household plumbing, not location, so every home should test for it." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El plomo depende de la plomería de la casa, no de la ubicación, por lo que todos los hogares deberían hacer un análisis de plomo."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Lead in well water usually comes from pipes, solder and well parts, not the rock, so it varies from house to house." : {
      "localizations" : {
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "machine_translated",
            "value" : "El plomo en el agua de pozo suele provenir de las tuberías, la soldadura y las piezas del pozo, no de la roca, por lo que varía de una casa a otra."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "Lead in well water usually comes from pipes, solder and well parts, not the rock. EPA's health goal for lead is zero, because no level is known to be safe." : {

    },
    "Lead usually comes from your plumbing, not the ground: old pipes, lead solder, and brass fittings or well parts. It varies from house to house." : {

    },
